// Enums.schema — all hand-declared enums for the unit.
// Aspect-oriented layout (SPEC §2): one aspect per file.
//
// NOTE (Glenn, 2026-08-05): some of these are flatbuffers residue — hand-declared
// only because flatbuffers gave no better tool. ShipType is really a DERIVED set
// (each ship config/asset defines a type), and when the Config/Assets layer
// lands, enums of that class are GENERATED from their definitions — the same
// set-extraction move as MessageType and ObjectType. Hand-declared enums remain
// for genuinely hand-owned sets (Team).

package example

enum Team      { None Red Blue }
enum CraftKind { None Light Medium Heavy }

// flatbuffers-residue class: eventually generated from Assets/Config definitions.
enum ShipType  { None Fighter Corvette Bomber Destroyer Carrier }

// demo-local, used by the switch idiom in Types.schema.
enum RecordKind { None Craft Debris }
